COMMENT ON TABLE client.account_team IS 'Maps agency-side personnel (account directors, strategists, planners, media buyers, creatives) to specific advertiser accounts. Captures assigned team member reference, role on account (Account Director, Strategic Planner, Media Lead, Creative Director), assignment start and end dates, FTE allocation percentage, primary contact flag, backup coverage, and team status. Enables resource planning, utilization tracking, conflict-of-interest checks, QBR preparation, and client-facing org chart generation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.account_team_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for each account team assignment record in the advertising agency. Serves as the primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser or agency-managed client account to which this team member is assigned. Anchors the assignment within the client domain hierarchy.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Account team assignments exist within the context of a formal agency-client relationship. Linking account_team to agency_relationship via agency_relationship_id allows the model to scope team assignme';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Account team members are assigned to cost centers for overhead allocation, utilization tracking, and P&L reporting. Essential for agency financial management to track labor costs by client account and LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.managed_supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Account team members often have vendor relationship management responsibilities—e.g., media buyer assigned to manage Google/Meta relationships for specific clients. Tracks vendor stewardship assignmen LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.account_access_level IS 'The level of access this team member has to the client account record in Salesforce CRM (read, edit, or all). Mirrors the Salesforce AccountTeamMember AccountAccessLevel field and governs data visibility for compliance and conflict-of-interest checks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.approval_date IS 'The date on which this account team assignment was formally approved by the designated approver. Used for governance audit trails and staffing compliance reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.assignment_code IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric code uniquely identifying this account team assignment, used in Workfront project management and Salesforce CRM for cross-system reference and QBR (Quarterly Business Review) reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.assignment_notes IS 'Free-text field capturing additional context about the team member''s assignment, such as special responsibilities, client preferences, transition notes, or coverage arrangements. Supports account management continuity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.assignment_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the team member''s assignment to the account. ''active'' indicates currently serving; ''on_leave'' indicates temporary absence with backup coverage; ''transitioning'' indicates handover in progress; ''inactive'' indicates assignment ended; ''pending'' indicates assignment approved but not yet started.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.assignment_type IS 'Classifies the nature of the team member''s assignment to the account: ''dedicated'' = exclusively assigned; ''shared'' = split across multiple accounts; ''project_based'' = assigned for a specific campaign or project; ''interim'' = temporary coverage assignment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.billing_rate_type IS 'Specifies the time unit basis for the billing rate applied to this team member''s account assignment (hourly, daily, monthly, or fixed fee). Determines how FTE allocation and time tracking translate to client invoicing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.billing_rate_usd IS 'The hourly or daily billing rate in USD applied to this team member''s time on the client account, as defined in the Statement of Work (SOW) or Master Service Agreement. Used for financial reconciliation and P&L reporting in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.client_facing_flag IS 'Indicates whether this team member has direct client-facing responsibilities and appears on the client-facing org chart. True = client-facing; False = internal/support role only. Governs inclusion in client communications and org chart generation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.conflict_of_interest_flag IS 'Indicates whether a potential conflict of interest has been identified for this team member''s assignment to the account (e.g., simultaneous assignment to a competing advertiser). True = conflict identified; False = no conflict. Triggers compliance review workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.conflict_review_date IS 'The date on which the most recent conflict-of-interest review was conducted for this team member''s account assignment. Supports compliance audit trails and periodic review scheduling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.conflict_review_outcome IS 'The outcome of the most recent conflict-of-interest review for this assignment. ''cleared'' = no conflict found; ''waived'' = conflict acknowledged and waived by client; ''escalated'' = referred to senior management; ''pending'' = review in progress.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.end_date IS 'The date on which the agency personnel member''s assignment to this client account is scheduled to end or actually ended. Null for open-ended assignments. Used for resource planning and transition management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.fte_allocation_pct IS 'The percentage of the team member''s full-time equivalent (FTE) capacity allocated to this specific client account, expressed as a decimal percentage (e.g., 50.00 = 50%). Supports resource utilization tracking, capacity planning, and P&L cost allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.is_backup_contact IS 'Indicates whether this team member serves as the backup coverage contact for the client account when the primary contact is unavailable. True = designated backup; False = not a backup. Supports continuity planning and leave coverage.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.is_primary_contact IS 'Indicates whether this team member is the designated primary point of contact for the client account. True = primary contact; False = supporting team member. Used for client-facing org chart generation and escalation routing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.last_review_date IS 'The date of the most recent formal review of this team member''s account assignment, typically conducted during QBR cycles or annual staffing reviews. Supports proactive account management and client satisfaction monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.next_review_date IS 'The scheduled date for the next formal review of this team member''s account assignment. Enables proactive scheduling of staffing reviews and QBR preparation cycles.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.org_chart_display_order IS 'Numeric sequence controlling the display order of this team member within the client-facing org chart for the account. Lower values appear first. Enables structured presentation of the account team hierarchy to clients.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.planned_hours_per_month IS 'The planned number of hours per month this team member is expected to dedicate to this client account, as agreed in the Statement of Work (SOW) or resource plan. Used for utilization tracking and capacity planning in Workfront.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.qbr_presenter_flag IS 'Indicates whether this team member is designated to present at the client''s Quarterly Business Review (QBR). True = QBR presenter; False = not a QBR presenter. Used for QBR preparation and client-facing agenda planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.role IS 'The functional role this agency personnel member holds on the client account (e.g., Account Director, Strategic Planner, Media Lead, Creative Director, Account Manager, Media Buyer). Drives org chart generation and responsibility mapping. Code set: ref.role.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.salesforce_team_member_code IS 'The unique identifier of the corresponding AccountTeamMember record in Salesforce CRM Sales Cloud. Supports CRM synchronization, client relationship management, and QBR preparation workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.seniority_level IS 'The seniority classification of the team member within their assigned role on this account (e.g., junior, mid, senior, lead, executive). Used for billing rate determination, resource planning, and QBR staffing reviews.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.start_date IS 'The date on which the agency personnel member formally began their assignment to this client account. Used for tenure tracking, utilization reporting, and conflict-of-interest checks.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.team_function IS 'The agency functional discipline this team member represents on the account (account management, media, creative, strategy, analytics, or PR). Enables cross-functional team composition reporting and resource planning by discipline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.account_team.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.agency_relationship IS 'Captures the formal relationship between the agency and an advertiser, including relationship type (AOR — Agency of Record, project-based, retainer, roster agency), relationship status, scope of services (media, creative, PR, digital, social), start and end dates, exclusivity flags, governing contract reference, and full relationship state-change history stored as effective-dated event records (AOR wins/losses, scope expansions, renewals, escalations, status transitions with effective dates, triggering events, previous state, new state, and narrative notes). This is the SSOT for both current relationship state and historical relationship lifecycle — no separate history table exists. Supports AOR tracking, pitch history, competitive conflict management, audit trail, and executive relationship lifecycle reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.agency_relationship_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the agency-advertiser relationship record. Primary key for this entity. Role classification: MASTER_AGREEMENT — represents a long-running formal binding relationship between the agency and an advertiser.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser or client organisation that is party to this agency relationship. Links to the client master record in the client domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the governing contract or Statement of Work (SOW) that formalises the terms of this agency relationship. Links to the contract master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.primary_supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Agency relationships often designate primary media suppliers or tech platforms used for that client account. Tracks which DSPs, SSPs, or publishers are approved/preferred under specific agency-client LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.annual_fee_amount IS 'The contracted annual agency fee or retainer amount in the agreed currency for this relationship. Used for P&L reporting, budget management, and financial reconciliation. Applicable for retainer and project-fee structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.aor_designation IS 'Specifies the specific Agency of Record (AOR) designation held by the agency for this client, if applicable. Distinguishes between full-service AOR and discipline-specific AOR designations (media, creative, digital, PR, social). Used for AOR tracking and executive relationship reporting. Code set: ref.aor_designation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.brand_scope IS 'Comma-delimited list of the client''s brand names or brand portfolio segments covered under this agency relationship. Distinguishes relationships that cover the full client portfolio from those scoped to specific brands or sub-brands.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.client_contact_email IS 'The business email address of the primary client contact for this relationship. Used for direct communication, meeting scheduling, and CRM record maintenance. Subject to GDPR and CCPA data protection requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.commission_rate_pct IS 'The agreed agency commission rate expressed as a percentage of gross media spend, applicable when the fee structure type is commission_based or hybrid. Used for financial reconciliation in Mediaocean Prisma and SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.competitive_conflict_flag IS 'Indicates whether this agency-client relationship involves a known competitive conflict with another client in the agency''s portfolio (i.e., the agency serves two competing advertisers in the same category). Critical for conflict management and new business governance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.conflict_category IS 'The product or industry category in which a competitive conflict exists, if the competitive conflict flag is true (e.g., ''Automotive'', ''Financial Services'', ''FMCG — Beverages''). Used for conflict management reporting and new business screening.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.crm_opportunity_code IS 'The external identifier of the corresponding Salesforce CRM Opportunity record that originated or tracks this agency-client relationship. Enables bi-directional traceability between the data lakehouse and the CRM system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.current_event_type IS 'The type of the most recent state-change event recorded against this relationship. Supports AOR win/loss tracking, scope change management, and executive relationship lifecycle reporting. Full event history is stored as effective-dated event records within this product. Code set: ref.current_event_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.effective_end_date IS 'The date on which the agency-client relationship is scheduled to end or was terminated. Nullable for open-ended relationships. Used for AOR tracking, renewal management, and competitive conflict management. Serves as EFFECTIVE_UNTIL for this MASTER_AGREEMENT entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.effective_start_date IS 'The date on which the agency-client relationship formally commenced and became binding. Used for AOR tracking, tenure calculations, and relationship lifecycle reporting. Serves as EFFECTIVE_FROM for this MASTER_AGREEMENT entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.estimated_annual_billings IS 'The estimated total annual media billings or revenue associated with this agency-client relationship, in the fee currency. Used for revenue forecasting, P&L reporting, and strategic account prioritisation. Distinct from the contracted annual fee amount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.event_effective_date IS 'The business-effective date of the most recent state-change event (e.g., the date an AOR win took effect, the date a scope expansion was agreed). Distinct from the record audit timestamp; used for effective-dated relationship lifecycle reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.event_notes IS 'Free-text narrative notes providing additional context for the most recent relationship state-change event. Captures qualitative detail such as client rationale, negotiation outcomes, or escalation context. Supports audit trail and executive relationship lifecycle reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.event_trigger IS 'A brief description of the business event or circumstance that triggered the most recent relationship state change (e.g., ''Client initiated competitive review'', ''Scope expanded to include social media'', ''Contract renewed for FY2025''). Supports narrative audit trail and executive reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.fee_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the annual fee amount and any financial values associated with this relationship (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Supports multi-currency financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.fee_structure_type IS 'The commercial fee model governing agency compensation under this relationship. Retainer_fee is a fixed recurring payment; commission_based is a percentage of media spend; project_fee is a one-time scoped payment; performance_based ties compensation to KPI outcomes; hybrid combines multiple models.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.geographic_scope IS 'The geographic markets or territories covered by this agency-client relationship (e.g., ''USA'', ''GBR,DEU,FRA'', ''Global''). Uses ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country codes where applicable. Supports multi-market AOR tracking and competitive conflict management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.incumbent_agency_name IS 'The name of the previous incumbent agency that held the account prior to this relationship being established, if applicable. Used for competitive intelligence, pitch history analysis, and AOR win/loss reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.is_exclusive IS 'Indicates whether the agency holds an exclusive mandate for the defined scope of services with this advertiser, preventing the client from engaging competing agencies for the same services. Critical for competitive conflict management and AOR governance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.lead_account_director IS 'The name of the senior agency account director who holds primary responsibility for managing this client relationship. Used for account team assignment, escalation routing, and executive relationship reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.mediaocean_client_code IS 'The client code assigned to this advertiser in Mediaocean Prisma, the media planning and buying system of record. Used for reconciliation of media plans, insertion orders (IOs), and billing records against this relationship.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.next_review_date IS 'The scheduled date of the next formal relationship review or Quarterly Business Review (QBR). Used for proactive account management, renewal planning, and executive calendar management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.notice_period_days IS 'The number of calendar days of advance written notice required by either party to terminate or materially modify this agency-client relationship, as specified in the governing contract or Statement of Work (SOW).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.pitch_type IS 'The type of pitch or selection process through which this agency-client relationship was established. Competitive_review is a formal multi-agency pitch; direct_award is a non-competitive appointment; incumbent_retention is a renewal without a formal pitch; rfi_rfp is a formal Request for Information (RFI) or Request for Proposal (RFP) process.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.pitch_win_date IS 'The date on which the agency formally won the pitch or competitive review that established this relationship. Used for pitch history tracking, new business reporting, and AOR win/loss analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.previous_relationship_status IS 'The relationship status immediately prior to the most recent state-change event. Stored alongside the current status to support audit trail requirements and state-transition reporting without requiring a separate history table.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.primary_client_contact IS 'The name of the primary contact person on the client/advertiser side for this relationship (e.g., CMO, Marketing Director, Brand Manager). Used for account management, communication routing, and CRM record maintenance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.relationship_code IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric business identifier for this agency-client relationship, used in Salesforce CRM, Mediaocean Prisma, and client-facing correspondence (e.g., REL-2024-00123). Serves as the BUSINESS_IDENTIFIER for this MASTER_AGREEMENT entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.relationship_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the agency-client relationship. Active indicates a live, operational engagement; pending indicates a relationship that has been agreed but not yet commenced; suspended indicates a temporary hold; terminated indicates the relationship has ended; under_review indicates a formal review or pitch process is underway. Serves as LIFECYCLE_STATUS for this MASTER_AGREEMENT entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.relationship_tier IS 'The strategic importance tier assigned to this agency-client relationship based on revenue, strategic value, and growth potential. Strategic denotes top-tier accounts receiving dedicated senior resources; key_account denotes significant accounts; standard denotes routine engagements; emerging denotes new or high-growth potential accounts.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.relationship_type IS 'Classification of the formal relationship structure between the agency and the advertiser. AOR (Agency of Record) denotes full-service exclusive mandate; project_based is scoped to a single campaign or deliverable; retainer is an ongoing fee-based engagement; roster_agency is a non-exclusive approved supplier; preferred_vendor is a qualified but non-exclusive partner. Serves as CLASSIFICATION_OR_TYPE for this MASTER_AGREEMENT entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.renewal_date IS 'The date on which the agency-client relationship contract is due for renewal or renegotiation. Distinct from the effective end date; used for proactive renewal pipeline management and AOR retention tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.review_cycle IS 'The agreed frequency at which the agency-client relationship is formally reviewed, including performance evaluation, scope assessment, and fee renegotiation. Supports Quarterly Business Review (QBR) scheduling and executive relationship lifecycle reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.scope_of_services IS 'Comma-delimited list of service disciplines covered under this relationship (e.g., media, creative, pr, digital, social, ooh, programmatic, sem, seo). Defines the breadth of the agency mandate and is used for competitive conflict management and scope expansion tracking. Code set: ref.scope_of_services.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.agency_relationship.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.client_brief IS 'Formal creative or campaign brief submitted by the client to initiate a new campaign, project, or creative deliverable. Captures brief title, brief type (campaign, creative, media, PR), submission date, requesting contact, target audience description, key message, mandatory inclusions, budget indication, desired KPIs, timeline requirements, and brief status (draft, approved, in-progress, closed). The SSOT for client-originated work requests.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.client_brief_id IS 'Unique system-generated identifier for the client brief record. Primary key for the client_brief data product.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.advertiser_id IS 'Identifier of the client (advertiser or agency) who submitted this brief. Links to the client master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: A client brief is submitted and executed within the scope of a formal agency-client relationship. Linking client_brief to agency_relationship via agency_relationship_id allows the agency to track whic';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.attribution_model_id IS 'Foreign key linking to performance.attribution_model. Business justification: Client briefs specify attribution requirements (e.g., ''use data-driven attribution, 30-day window''). Media planners reference the brief-specified attribution model when configuring campaigns. This lin LOGICAL REF -> adserver_db.performance.attribution_model.attribution_model_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: A client brief is typically scoped to a specific brand within the advertiser''s portfolio. Adding client_brand_id to client_brief enables brand-level campaign brief tracking, allowing the agency to man';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Client briefs initiate projects/initiatives that are tracked in project management systems. Currently workfront_project_id is stored as an unlinked string. Normalizing to initiative_id FK enables join LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.segment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.segment. Business justification: Campaign briefs specify target audience segments for media planning and activation. This is the primary mechanism linking client requirements to targetable audiences in advertising operations. Essenti LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.segment.segment_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Briefs frequently specify preferred suppliers/publishers for campaign execution. Media planners reference approved vendor lists when briefing campaigns. Essential for RFP routing and vendor selection LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.target_persona_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.persona. Business justification: Briefs reference personas to guide creative strategy, messaging, and channel selection. Standard practice in advertising where personas inform campaign development beyond just segment targeting. Suppo LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.persona.persona_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.approval_date IS 'Calendar date on which the brief was formally approved by the agency account team and accepted for execution. Null if not yet approved.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.brand_guidelines_version IS 'Version identifier of the client brand guidelines document that must be adhered to for all creative executions under this brief (e.g., ''v3.2'', ''2024-Q1''). Ensures creative compliance with current brand standards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.brief_number IS 'Externally-visible, human-readable reference number assigned to the brief at submission (e.g., BRF-2024-000123). Used in client communications, Workfront project creation, and Mediaocean Prisma work orders.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.brief_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the client brief. Drives workflow routing: draft (being authored), submitted (awaiting review), approved (accepted for execution), in_progress (active work underway), on_hold (paused), closed (completed or cancelled).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.brief_type IS 'Classification of the brief by the type of work being requested. Determines the downstream workflow and team assignment. Code set: ref.brief_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.budget_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the budget indication amount (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Supports multi-currency client engagements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.budget_indication_amount IS 'Client-indicated total budget for the campaign or project described in this brief, expressed in the operating currency. This is a directional figure provided at brief stage, not a committed spend. Used for resource planning and scoping.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.campaign_end_date IS 'Client-requested end date for the campaign or deliverable described in the brief. Defines the desired flight window.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.campaign_objective IS 'Primary marketing objective the client wants to achieve with this campaign or project. Drives KPI selection and channel strategy. Code set: ref.campaign_objective.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.campaign_start_date IS 'Client-requested start date for the campaign or deliverable described in the brief. Represents the desired go-live date as specified by the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.channel_requirements IS 'Client-specified media channels or platforms required or preferred for this campaign (e.g., CTV, DOOH, OTT, social, search, OOH, programmatic). Free-text to capture complex multi-channel requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.closed_date IS 'Date on which the brief was formally closed, either upon successful completion of all deliverables or cancellation. Null if the brief is still active. Supports lifecycle reporting and pipeline analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.closure_reason IS 'Reason code explaining why the brief was closed. Populated when brief_status transitions to ''closed''. Supports win/loss analysis and client relationship management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.competitive_context IS 'Client-provided description of the competitive landscape relevant to this campaign, including key competitors, market positioning, and Share of Voice (SOV) considerations. Confidential business intelligence.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.creative_format_requirements IS 'Specific creative formats, sizes, or specifications required by the client (e.g., IAB standard banner sizes, VAST video specs, print dimensions). Informs creative production scope.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.deliverable_due_date IS 'Client-specified deadline by which the primary deliverable (creative, media plan, strategy deck, etc.) must be completed and delivered. May differ from campaign start date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.geographic_scope IS 'Description of the geographic markets or regions targeted by this campaign (e.g., national, specific DMAs, countries). Free-text to support complex geo-targeting requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.is_agency_managed IS 'Indicates whether this brief is submitted through an intermediary agency on behalf of the end advertiser (True) or directly by the advertiser (False). Affects billing, reporting, and account team assignment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.is_confidential IS 'Indicates whether the client has designated this brief as confidential, restricting access to named account team members only. Drives data access controls and document handling procedures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.key_message IS 'The primary communication message or value proposition the client wants to convey to the target audience. Core creative direction provided in the brief.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.mandatory_exclusions IS 'Client-specified elements, themes, competitors, or content that must NOT appear in any deliverable. Includes brand safety restrictions and competitive separation requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.mandatory_inclusions IS 'Client-specified elements that must appear in all creative executions or deliverables (e.g., legal disclaimers, brand taglines, product claims, regulatory copy, logo usage requirements).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.primary_kpi IS 'The single most important Key Performance Indicator (KPI) the client will use to measure campaign success. Drives optimization strategy and reporting requirements. Code set: ref.primary_kpi.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.primary_kpi_target_value IS 'Numeric target value the client expects to achieve for the primary KPI (e.g., a CTR of 0.0250 means 2.5%, a CPM of 5.00 means $5.00 per thousand impressions). Precision to 4 decimal places supports rate-based KPIs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.priority_level IS 'Client or account team-assigned priority level for this brief, used to triage work intake and allocate agency resources. Drives scheduling in Workfront project management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.regulatory_compliance_notes IS 'Client-specified regulatory, legal, or compliance requirements that must be observed in all deliverables (e.g., GDPR consent requirements, CCPA disclosures, FTC endorsement guidelines, industry-specific advertising restrictions).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.revision_reason IS 'Narrative explanation of why the brief was revised from a prior version. Populated when brief_version > 1. Supports change management and audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.salesforce_opportunity_code IS 'Reference identifier of the associated Salesforce CRM Opportunity record, linking the brief to the revenue pipeline and account management context.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.submission_date IS 'Calendar date on which the client formally submitted the brief to the agency. The principal business event date for this record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.title IS 'Short, descriptive title of the client brief as provided by the requesting client contact (e.g., ''Q3 2024 Summer Campaign Launch Brief'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.version IS 'Incrementing version number of the brief document, starting at 1. Incremented each time the client submits a revised brief. Supports brief revision history and change management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.client_brief.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.revenue_target IS 'Annual and quarterly revenue targets set for each advertiser account, broken down by service line (media, creative, digital, PR). Captures target period, target amount, currency, service line, target type (gross revenue, net revenue, fee income), target owner (account director), and target status. Supports P&L management, QBR preparation, and account growth planning. Distinct from actual billed revenue owned by the finance domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.revenue_target_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for each client revenue target record. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the advertiser account for which this revenue target is set. Links to the client.advertiser master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Revenue targets are set in the context of a specific agency-client relationship. Linking revenue_target to agency_relationship via agency_relationship_id allows finance and account management teams to';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.agreement_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.agreement. Business justification: Revenue targets are set at the master agreement level in advertising — account teams forecast billings against contracted agreements. Agreement-level revenue attainment reporting and pipeline-to-contr';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Revenue targets in advertising agencies are frequently set at brand level within advertiser accounts, not just advertiser-level. Enables brand-specific revenue forecasting, pipeline management, accoun';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Revenue targets are managed and reported by cost center for management accounting and variance analysis. `cost_centre_code` is a denormalized text reference to the cost_center entity; replacing it wit LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Revenue targets drive budget allocation decisions and resource planning. Account directors set client revenue targets that inform budget approvals, headcount planning, and investment decisions for cli LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Agency revenue targets are set against specific initiatives (pitch wins, project scopes). Linking enables tracking of actual project revenue vs. targets — a core agency financial management and accoun LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Revenue targets in advertising are set against specific contracted SOWs. SOW-level revenue attainment tracking — comparing target vs. actual billings against contracted scope — is a core account manag';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.account_growth_rate_pct IS 'The year-over-year or period-over-period percentage growth rate embedded in this target relative to the prior comparable period''s target. Expressed as a decimal (e.g., 0.1500 = 15%). Used in account growth planning and QBR target-setting rationale.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.approval_date IS 'The date on which the revenue target was formally approved by the designated approver. Marks the transition from pending_approval to approved status and is used in audit trails for P&L governance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.confidence_level IS 'Account team''s assessed confidence in achieving this revenue target: high (strong pipeline, contracted SOW coverage), medium (pipeline in progress, partial SOW coverage), low (speculative, dependent on new business wins). Used in risk-adjusted P&L forecasting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.contracted_sow_coverage_pct IS 'The proportion of the revenue target already covered by signed Statements of Work (SOW) or Insertion Orders (IO) at the time of target setting or last update. Expressed as a decimal (e.g., 0.6500 = 65%). Supports pipeline risk assessment and P&L confidence scoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.crm_opportunity_code IS 'The Salesforce CRM Sales Cloud Opportunity record ID linked to this revenue target, where the target originates from or is tracked against a specific sales opportunity. Enables traceability from target to pipeline to closed-won revenue.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code in which the target_amount is denominated (e.g., USD, GBP, EUR). Supports multi-currency advertiser portfolios and cross-market P&L consolidation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.fiscal_quarter IS 'The fiscal quarter to which this target applies (Q1–Q4). Populated when target_period_type is ''quarterly''; null for annual targets. Used in QBR preparation and quarterly pacing analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.fiscal_year IS 'The four-digit fiscal year to which this revenue target applies (e.g., 2025). Aligns with the SAP S/4HANA FI fiscal year calendar for P&L management and budget reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.fx_rate_applied IS 'The exchange rate used to convert target_amount to target_amount_usd at the time of target creation or last revision. Stored for auditability and variance analysis when FX rates fluctuate during the target period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.is_stretch_target IS 'Indicates whether this target is designated as a stretch (aspirational) target above the base committed target. True = stretch target used for incentive compensation modelling; False = base committed target used for P&L planning. Supports Workday HCM talent performance review and bonus calculation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.notes IS 'Free-text field for account team commentary on the revenue target, including assumptions, dependencies, client commitments, or QBR talking points. Not used for structured data; supports qualitative context in account growth planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.original_target_amount IS 'The initial revenue target amount set at the start of the period before any revisions. Preserved for variance analysis comparing original plan vs. revised plan vs. actual billed revenue. Populated only when revision_number > 0.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.period_end_date IS 'The calendar date on which the revenue target period ends. Defines the boundary for target attainment measurement and QBR reporting cycles.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.period_start_date IS 'The calendar date on which the revenue target period begins. Used to align target pacing with actual billed revenue from the finance domain and to support time-series analytics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.pipeline_amount IS 'The total value of identified but not yet contracted revenue opportunities in the Salesforce CRM pipeline that are expected to contribute to this target. Distinct from target_amount (the committed plan) and actual billed revenue. Supports gap-to-target analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.profit_centre_code IS 'SAP S/4HANA CO profit centre code associated with this revenue target, enabling segment-level P&L reporting by business unit, geography, or service line. Supports EBITDA reporting and management accounting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.revision_number IS 'Sequential integer indicating how many times this revenue target has been revised (0 = original). Enables version tracking of target changes throughout the fiscal period, supporting variance analysis between original and revised targets.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.revision_reason IS 'Free-text explanation for why the revenue target was revised (e.g., client budget reduction, scope expansion, new service line added, market conditions). Supports QBR narrative and P&L variance commentary.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.roas_target IS 'The target Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) ratio associated with this revenue target, where applicable (primarily for performance-based media service lines). Expressed as a multiplier (e.g., 4.0000 = $4 revenue per $1 ad spend). Used in digital performance optimization and KPI alignment with The Trade Desk programmatic buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.service_line IS 'The agency service line to which this revenue target is attributed: media (Media Planning and Buying), creative (Creative Development and Production), digital (Digital Marketing and Performance Optimization), pr (Public Relations and Communications), analytics (Data Analytics and Audience Insights), strategy (Brand Strategy and Positioning). Enables service-line-level P&L reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_amount IS 'The gross or net revenue target value set for the advertiser account for the specified period and service line, expressed in the currency defined by currency_code. This is the planned figure; actual billed revenue is owned by the finance domain. Core input for P&L management and account growth planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_amount_usd IS 'The revenue target amount converted to US Dollars (USD) using the exchange rate applied at the time of target setting. Enables cross-currency portfolio aggregation and global P&L reporting without requiring runtime FX conversion.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_code IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric business identifier for this revenue target record, used in Quarterly Business Review (QBR) reporting, P&L management, and cross-system reconciliation with SAP S/4HANA CO module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_name IS 'Human-readable label for this revenue target, typically combining the advertiser name, service line, and target period (e.g., ''Acme Corp — Media — FY2025 Q1''). Used in QBR decks and account growth planning documents.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_owner_name IS 'Display name of the account director or account manager who owns this revenue target. Stored denormalized for reporting convenience in QBR decks and P&L dashboards without requiring a join to the talent domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_period_type IS 'Granularity of the target period: annual (full fiscal year), quarterly (fiscal quarter), or monthly (calendar month). Determines how the target_amount is interpreted and how actuals are paced against it in QBR reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_setting_method IS 'The methodology used to derive this revenue target: top_down (allocated from agency-level P&L plan), bottom_up (built from individual campaign and SOW estimates), negotiated (agreed bilaterally with client), market_indexed (benchmarked against market growth indices such as Nielsen Ad Intel competitive data).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the revenue target record. draft: being authored; pending_approval: submitted for sign-off; approved: signed off by account director and finance; active: in-period and being tracked; revised: superseded by a revised target; closed: period ended; cancelled: target withdrawn. Code set: ref.target_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.target_type IS 'Classification of the revenue target by income recognition method: gross_revenue (total billings before agency commission deduction), net_revenue (billings net of media costs), fee_income (project or retainer fees), commission_income (media commission earned), retainer_fee (recurring fixed-fee arrangement). Drives P&L line allocation in SAP S/4HANA FI.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.revenue_target.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.advertiser IS 'Master record for every advertiser (direct client or agency-managed brand) that the agency serves. Captures authoritative identity including legal entity name, trading name, industry vertical (IAB taxonomy), business segment, holding company affiliation, CRM account ID (Salesforce), ERP customer number (SAP), tax identifiers (VAT/EIN), incorporation jurisdiction, credit terms, payment terms, preferred currency, account status (prospect, active, dormant, churned), account tier, and all engagement preferences (preferred communication channels, reporting cadence, invoice delivery method, language preference, time zone, approval workflow preferences, GDPR/CCPA data sharing consent flags). Also stores structured address records (registered office, billing address, shipping address, regional offices) with address type, full postal details, country (ISO 3166), geocoordinates, and validation status. This is the SSOT for advertiser identity, commercial configuration, engagement preferences, and physical/mailing addresses across the entire data model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.advertiser_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for the advertiser record. Primary key for the advertiser master data product. Role: MASTER_PARTY.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.iab_taxonomy_id IS 'Foreign key linking to audience.taxonomy. Business justification: DSP and DMP onboarding requires advertisers to be classified against IAB audience taxonomy for targeting eligibility and privacy compliance. ''iab_industry_vertical'' is a denormalized text representati LOGICAL REF -> cdp_db.audience.taxonomy.taxonomy_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.account_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the advertiser account. Drives workflow routing, reporting segmentation, and CRM pipeline management. ''prospect'' = pre-contract; ''active'' = live campaigns; ''dormant'' = no recent activity; ''churned'' = relationship ended; ''suspended'' = temporarily on hold.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.account_tier IS 'Commercial tier classification of the advertiser based on revenue contribution, strategic importance, and engagement level. Determines service level, dedicated account team assignment, and reporting cadence. Aligns with agency tiering models used in account management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.address_validation_status IS 'Indicates the validation status of the advertiser''s billing address against a postal address verification service. ''validated'' = confirmed deliverable; ''unvalidated'' = not yet checked; ''failed'' = address could not be verified; ''pending'' = verification in progress. Used in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma billing workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.approval_workflow_type IS 'Defines the creative and campaign approval workflow configuration for this advertiser. ''single_approver'' = one designated approver; ''multi_approver'' = sequential or parallel approval chain; ''auto_approve'' = pre-authorized for specific asset types. Configured in Workfront proofing module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.ccpa_consent_flag IS 'Indicates whether the advertiser has opted in to data sharing under CCPA regulations. True = data sharing permitted; False = opt-out or not applicable. Applicable for California-based advertisers and campaigns targeting California consumers. Drives NAI and TAG compliance controls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.churn_date IS 'The date on which the advertiser''s account was marked as churned (relationship ended). Populated only when account_status = ''churned''. Used for churn analysis, win-back campaign targeting, and P&L impact reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.credit_terms IS 'The agreed payment credit terms for this advertiser, defining the number of days after invoice date by which payment is due. Configured in SAP S/4HANA AR and Mediaocean Prisma for billing workflows. Drives cash flow forecasting and P&L management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.crm_account_code IS 'The unique account identifier assigned to this advertiser in Salesforce CRM (Sales Cloud). Serves as the cross-system join key between the lakehouse Silver Layer and the CRM system of record for account management and client services.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.ein IS 'The US federal Employer Identification Number (EIN) assigned by the IRS to the advertiser. Used for US tax reporting, W-9 compliance, and financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA. Applicable for US-incorporated entities.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.erp_customer_number IS 'The customer master number assigned to this advertiser in SAP S/4HANA (FI/AR module). Used for billing, accounts receivable, and financial reconciliation processes. Links advertiser identity to financial transactions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.gdpr_consent_flag IS 'Indicates whether the advertiser has provided explicit consent for data sharing and processing under GDPR. True = consent granted; False = consent not granted or withdrawn. Mandatory for EU-based advertisers and any data processing involving EU data subjects. Drives data governance controls.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.holding_company_name IS 'The name of the parent holding company or corporate group to which this advertiser belongs (e.g., WPP, Publicis, Omnicom client-side equivalent). Used for consolidated billing, conflict-of-interest checks, and group-level revenue reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.incorporation_jurisdiction IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 or alpha-3 country code of the jurisdiction in which the advertiser''s legal entity is incorporated. Used for regulatory compliance, tax treatment, and contract law determination. Examples: ''US'', ''GB'', ''DEU''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.invoice_delivery_method IS 'The preferred method by which invoices are delivered to the advertiser. Drives automated invoice dispatch workflows in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma. ''edi'' = Electronic Data Interchange for enterprise clients with automated AP systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.is_agency_managed IS 'Indicates whether this advertiser is managed through an intermediary agency relationship (True) or is a direct client of the agency (False). Determines billing structure, IO (Insertion Order) routing, and account team assignment in Mediaocean Prisma and Salesforce CRM.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.language_preference IS 'The advertiser''s preferred language for communications, reports, and invoices, expressed as an IETF BCP 47 language tag (e.g., ''en-US'', ''fr-FR'', ''de-DE''). Drives localization in Salesforce Marketing Cloud and report generation workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.legal_entity_name IS 'The full registered legal name of the advertiser as recorded with the relevant incorporation authority. Used for contracts, invoices, and regulatory filings. Maps to Salesforce CRM Account Name (legal) and SAP S/4HANA customer master legal name.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.managing_agency_name IS 'Name of the intermediary agency managing this advertiser''s account, if is_agency_managed is True. Used for IO routing, commission calculations, and agency-of-record (AOR) tracking in Mediaocean Prisma and Salesforce CRM.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.onboarding_date IS 'The date on which the advertiser was formally onboarded as a client of the agency. Marks the start of the commercial relationship. Used for tenure calculations, anniversary-based QBR scheduling, and cohort analysis in analytics workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.payment_terms IS 'The agreed payment method/instrument for this advertiser''s invoices. Distinct from credit_terms (which defines timing); this defines the payment channel/instrument. Configured in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma for financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.preferred_comm_channel IS 'The advertiser''s preferred channel for day-to-day account communications and notifications. Used to route alerts, campaign updates, and approval requests in Salesforce CRM and Workfront project management workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.preferred_currency IS 'The ISO 4217 three-letter currency code representing the advertiser''s preferred billing and reporting currency (e.g., ''USD'', ''EUR'', ''GBP''). Used in Mediaocean Prisma for media billing and SAP S/4HANA for invoicing and financial reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.primary_contact_email IS 'The primary email address of the advertiser''s main point of contact at the client organization. Used for campaign communications, reporting delivery, and account management correspondence. Sourced from Salesforce CRM Contact object.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.primary_contact_name IS 'Full name of the advertiser''s primary point of contact at the client organization. Used in account management, QBR preparation, and client services workflows. Sourced from Salesforce CRM Contact object.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.primary_contact_phone IS 'Primary telephone number for the advertiser''s main point of contact. Used for urgent campaign communications and account management. Stored in E.164 international format. Sourced from Salesforce CRM Contact object.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.registered_office_country IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code for the country where the advertiser''s registered office is located. May differ from billing address country. Used for regulatory compliance, GDPR/CCPA applicability determination, and legal jurisdiction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.reporting_cadence IS 'The agreed frequency at which performance reports and analytics dashboards are delivered to the advertiser. Drives automated report scheduling in Google Campaign Manager 360 and analytics workflows. Aligns with QBR (Quarterly Business Review) planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.time_zone IS 'The advertiser''s primary operational time zone expressed as an IANA Time Zone Database identifier (e.g., ''America/New_York'', ''Europe/London''). Used for scheduling campaign flights, reporting cadence, and meeting coordination in Workfront and Salesforce CRM.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.trading_name IS 'The brand or ''doing business as'' (DBA) name under which the advertiser operates commercially. May differ from the legal entity name. Used in campaign documentation, media plans, and client-facing materials.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.vat_number IS 'The advertiser''s Value Added Tax (VAT) registration number issued by the relevant tax authority. Required for EU/UK invoicing compliance and cross-border tax treatment. Stored for financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA FI module.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.advertiser_hierarchy IS 'Defines the parent-child organizational hierarchy among advertiser entities — holding company, subsidiary, brand, and sub-brand relationships. Supports multi-level account trees for large conglomerates (e.g., WPP, Publicis clients) where billing, reporting, and campaign attribution must roll up through corporate structures. Tracks hierarchy type (holding, subsidiary, brand portfolio), effective dates, and consolidation flags.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.advertiser_hierarchy_id IS 'Unique surrogate identifier for each advertiser hierarchy relationship record. Serves as the primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.child_advertiser_id IS 'Identifier of the child advertiser entity in the hierarchy (e.g., subsidiary, brand, or sub-brand). References the advertiser entity that sits one level below the parent in the corporate tree.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Holding company and advertiser hierarchy nodes map to consolidated billing cost centers for group-level P&L rollup and consolidated invoice reporting. Finance teams require this link to perform hierar LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.parent_advertiser_id IS 'Identifier of the parent advertiser entity in the hierarchy (e.g., holding company or parent subsidiary). References the advertiser entity that sits one level above the child in the corporate tree.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.primary_root_advertiser_id IS 'Identifier of the ultimate holding company or top-level entity in the advertiser corporate tree. Enables direct roll-up to the conglomerate level for consolidated billing, SOV analysis, and enterprise reporting without traversing the full hierarchy path.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.agency_commission_rate IS 'The negotiated agency commission rate (expressed as a decimal, e.g., 0.1500 for 15%) applicable to media buys placed on behalf of the child entity within this hierarchy. Stored at the hierarchy level to support tiered commission structures for holding company clients in Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the account management or finance authority who approved the establishment or modification of this hierarchy relationship. Required for governance and SOW compliance in client services workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.approved_date IS 'The date on which this hierarchy relationship was formally approved by the designated account management or finance authority. Distinct from the effective start date — approval may precede the operational effective date.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.billing_consolidation_flag IS 'Indicates whether invoices and media spend for the child entity are consolidated and billed through the parent entity. Distinct from the general consolidation flag — specifically governs Mediaocean Prisma billing workflows and Insertion Order (IO) aggregation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.change_reason IS 'Categorized reason code explaining why this hierarchy relationship record was created or last modified. Supports audit trail requirements and change management reporting for account management teams during corporate restructuring events. Code set: ref.change_reason.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.consolidation_flag IS 'Indicates whether the child entity''s spend, impressions, and campaign performance metrics should be financially consolidated into the parent entity''s reporting and P&L. Critical for holding company clients where subsidiary budgets roll up to a master account in SAP S/4HANA CO.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.country_code IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 three-letter country code of the primary operating jurisdiction for this hierarchy relationship. Used to apply correct regulatory reporting requirements (GDPR, CCPA, FTC), tax treatment in SAP S/4HANA, and local media buying rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.crm_hierarchy_code IS 'The native account hierarchy relationship identifier from Salesforce CRM Sales Cloud. Enables bi-directional synchronization between the lakehouse silver layer and the CRM system of record for account management and client services workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the billing and financial consolidation currency applicable to this hierarchy relationship (e.g., ''USD'', ''EUR'', ''GBP''). Governs how media spend and agency fees are consolidated in Mediaocean Prisma and SAP S/4HANA FI.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.data_sharing_consent_flag IS 'Indicates whether the child advertiser entity has provided consent for audience data and campaign performance data to be shared with the parent entity in this hierarchy. Critical for GDPR and CCPA compliance when consolidating audience insights across corporate structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.effective_end_date IS 'The date on which this parent-child hierarchy relationship ceases to be operationally effective. Nullable for open-ended relationships. Supports temporal hierarchy versioning when corporate structures change due to divestitures or rebranding.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.effective_start_date IS 'The date on which this parent-child hierarchy relationship became or becomes operationally effective. Used to enforce temporally accurate billing roll-ups and campaign attribution when corporate structures change (e.g., acquisition effective date).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_code IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric business code uniquely identifying this parent-child hierarchy relationship. Used in Mediaocean Prisma and Salesforce CRM for cross-system reconciliation and billing roll-up references.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_description IS 'Free-text narrative describing the business context, rationale, or special conditions of this parent-child hierarchy relationship. Captures nuances such as regional carve-outs, brand licensing arrangements, or joint venture structures not fully expressed by the type and role fields.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_level IS 'Numeric depth of the child advertiser entity within the corporate account tree, where level 1 represents the ultimate holding company. Enables multi-level roll-up queries for consolidated P&L and campaign reporting across conglomerates such as WPP or Publicis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_name IS 'Human-readable label describing this specific parent-child hierarchy relationship (e.g., ''Unilever > Dove Brand Portfolio''). Used in account management dashboards, QBR presentations, and client services reporting for clear identification of the relationship.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_path IS 'Materialized slash-delimited path string representing the full ancestry chain from the root holding company to the current child node (e.g., ''/HoldCo/SubsidiaryA/BrandX''). Supports efficient subtree queries and lineage tracing in Databricks without recursive CTEs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the parent-child hierarchy relationship. Drives whether the relationship is used for active campaign attribution, billing consolidation, and reporting roll-ups in Mediaocean Prisma and Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.hierarchy_type IS 'Classifies the nature of the parent-child relationship within the advertiser corporate structure. Determines how billing, reporting, and campaign attribution roll up through the account tree. Code set: ref.hierarchy_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.industry_sector IS 'The IAB Content Taxonomy industry sector classification of the child advertiser entity within this hierarchy (e.g., ''Consumer Packaged Goods'', ''Automotive'', ''Financial Services''). Supports audience segmentation, competitive SOV analysis, and Nielsen Ad Intel competitive monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.is_primary_hierarchy IS 'Indicates whether this relationship represents the primary (canonical) hierarchy path for the child advertiser entity. When an entity belongs to multiple hierarchy trees (e.g., matrix structures), this flag identifies the authoritative roll-up path for billing and consolidated reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.market_region IS 'The geographic market region in which this hierarchy relationship is operationally active (e.g., ''North America'', ''EMEA'', ''APAC''). Determines applicable regulatory frameworks (GDPR, CCPA), media buying practices, and regional account team assignments. Code set: ref.market_region.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.ownership_percentage IS 'The percentage of ownership the parent entity holds in the child entity (0.00–100.00). Used to determine proportional financial consolidation thresholds and to classify the relationship as majority-owned, minority-owned, or affiliated for P&L reporting in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.prisma_hierarchy_code IS 'The native account hierarchy identifier from Mediaocean Prisma used for media planning, buying, and billing roll-up. Supports reconciliation between the lakehouse and Prisma for consolidated media spend reporting across the advertiser corporate tree.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.relationship_role IS 'Describes the commercial or legal role of the child entity relative to the parent within the hierarchy (e.g., wholly-owned subsidiary vs. franchise vs. joint venture). Informs contract and billing treatment in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.reporting_consolidation_flag IS 'Indicates whether campaign performance data (impressions, clicks, CTR, ROAS) for the child entity rolls up into the parent entity''s consolidated reporting dashboards in Google Campaign Manager 360 and The Trade Desk. May differ from billing consolidation in matrix account structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.source_system IS 'Identifies the operational system of record from which this hierarchy relationship record was originally sourced or is mastered. Supports data lineage tracking and conflict resolution when the same hierarchy is maintained across multiple systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.sov_rollup_flag IS 'Indicates whether the child entity''s media spend and impressions should be included in the parent entity''s Share of Voice (SOV) calculations for competitive analysis in Nielsen Ad Intel and Comscore. Enables accurate conglomerate-level SOV reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.version_number IS 'Monotonically incrementing version counter for this hierarchy relationship record. Incremented each time the hierarchy definition is modified (e.g., ownership percentage change, status update). Supports optimistic concurrency control and audit trail reconstruction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.advertiser_hierarchy.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE client.brand IS 'Represents an individual brand owned by an advertiser. A single advertiser may manage multiple brands (e.g., Unilever owns Dove, Axe, Lipton). Captures brand name, brand code, category, sub-category, brand tier, launch date, brand status, and the owning advertiser. Serves as the SSOT for brand identity referenced by campaigns, creative assets, and media plans. Distinct from the brand domain''s brand strategy and positioning entities.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_id IS 'Unique identifier for the brand. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Brand-level P&L reporting and internal cost allocation require each client brand to map to a finance cost center. Agency finance teams run brand profitability reports by cost center; this link is stan LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.primary_client_brand_advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the parent advertiser (client) who owns this brand. A single advertiser may own multiple brands (e.g., Unilever owns Dove, Axe, Lipton).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.annual_media_budget IS 'The total approved annual media spend budget allocated to this brand in the base currency. Used for budget pacing, media plan authorization, and Profit & Loss (P&L) reporting in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_category IS 'Primary product or service category the brand competes in (e.g., Personal Care, Food & Beverage, Automotive, Financial Services). Aligns with IAB Content Taxonomy for audience targeting and competitive analysis. Code set: ref.brand_category.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_code IS 'Externally-known alphanumeric short code uniquely identifying the brand across operational systems including Google Campaign Manager 360, Mediaocean Prisma, and The Trade Desk. Used for trafficking, billing, and reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_description IS 'Free-text narrative describing the brand''s identity, value proposition, target audience, and key differentiators. Used by account teams, creative teams, and media planners to ensure brand-consistent execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_name IS 'The official commercial name of the brand as recognized in the market (e.g., Dove, Axe, Lipton). Used as the primary human-readable identifier across campaigns, creative assets, and media plans.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the brand record. Controls whether the brand is eligible for campaign assignment, media planning, and creative production. ''pending_launch'' indicates a brand approved but not yet publicly launched.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.brand_tier IS 'Strategic positioning tier of the brand within the advertiser''s portfolio, indicating relative market positioning and investment priority. Drives media budget allocation, creative production standards, and account team resourcing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.budget_currency IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the brand''s annual media budget (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Required for multi-currency financial reconciliation in SAP S/4HANA and Mediaocean Prisma.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.crm_brand_code IS 'The brand''s unique identifier in Salesforce CRM (Sales Cloud / Marketing Cloud). Enables cross-system reconciliation between the lakehouse Silver Layer and the operational CRM system of record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.dam_folder_code IS 'The folder or collection identifier in Workfront DAM (Digital Asset Management) where all creative assets for this brand are stored. Enables direct navigation from brand record to associated creative library.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.data_privacy_classification IS 'Privacy classification governing data collection and audience targeting practices for this brand. ''children'' applies COPPA/GDPR-K restrictions. ''sensitive'' applies enhanced consent requirements under GDPR Article 9 and CCPA. Drives audience data usage policies in the DMP/CDP.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.digital_advertising_enabled IS 'Indicates whether the brand is approved and configured for digital advertising including programmatic, paid search (PPC/SEM), and social media. Controls eligibility for The Trade Desk DSP activation and Google Campaign Manager 360 trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.discontinuation_date IS 'The date on which the brand was officially discontinued or retired from the market. Null for active brands. Used to enforce data governance rules preventing new campaign assignments to discontinued brands.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.guidelines_url IS 'URL pointing to the brand''s official style guide and creative guidelines document stored in Workfront DAM or Adobe Creative Cloud. Used by creative teams to ensure brand-consistent asset production.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.is_house_brand IS 'Indicates whether this brand is an agency house brand or proprietary brand (True) versus a client-owned advertiser brand (False). Affects revenue recognition, conflict-of-interest checks, and P&L attribution in SAP S/4HANA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.launch_date IS 'The date on which the brand was officially launched in the market. Used for brand age calculations, anniversary campaign planning, and historical performance benchmarking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.nielsen_brand_code IS 'The brand identifier assigned by Nielsen Ad Intel for competitive monitoring, audience measurement, and Gross Rating Point (GRP) tracking. Enables competitive spend benchmarking and Share of Voice (SOV) analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.operating_markets IS 'Comma-separated list of ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country codes representing all markets where the brand is actively sold and advertised. Used for multi-market campaign planning, regulatory compliance scoping, and global media buying via The Trade Desk.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.portfolio_rank IS 'Numeric rank of the brand within the advertiser''s portfolio based on strategic importance and revenue contribution (1 = highest priority). Used for resource allocation, account team staffing, and Quarterly Business Review (QBR) prioritization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.primary_channel IS 'The primary media channel through which the brand predominantly advertises. Drives default media planning templates in Mediaocean Prisma and channel-specific KPI frameworks. OOH = Out-of-Home.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.primary_market_country IS 'ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 country code representing the brand''s primary operating market (e.g., USA, GBR, DEU). Drives regulatory compliance requirements (GDPR, CCPA), media planning geography, and reporting currency selection.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.prisma_brand_code IS 'The brand identifier used in Mediaocean Prisma for media planning, buying, billing, and financial reconciliation. Ensures accurate budget allocation and invoice matching at the brand level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.programmatic_eligible IS 'Indicates whether the brand is approved for Real-Time Bidding (RTB) and programmatic media buying via Demand-Side Platforms (DSPs) such as The Trade Desk. Brands may be excluded due to regulatory restrictions, brand safety policies, or client preference.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.regulatory_restrictions IS 'Free-text description of any regulatory or legal advertising restrictions applicable to the brand (e.g., alcohol advertising watershed rules, pharmaceutical fair balance requirements, gambling advertising restrictions). Informs creative compliance review and media placement approvals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.safety_level IS 'The brand safety classification tier governing content adjacency restrictions for programmatic and digital media buying. Determines keyword blocklists, content category exclusions, and inventory quality thresholds applied in The Trade Desk and Google Campaign Manager 360.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.sov_target_pct IS 'The client-agreed target Share of Voice (SOV) percentage for this brand within its competitive category. Used as a KPI benchmark for media planning, campaign performance evaluation, and Nielsen Ad Intel competitive monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.sub_category IS 'Secondary classification within the brand category providing finer segmentation (e.g., within Personal Care: Skin Care, Hair Care, Deodorants). Supports audience insights, competitive benchmarking via Nielsen Ad Intel, and media planning.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.tagline IS 'The official marketing tagline or slogan associated with the brand (e.g., ''Just Do It'', ''Real Beauty''). Stored as a reference for creative consistency checks and brand compliance reviews.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.website_url IS 'The official public-facing website URL for the brand. Used for digital campaign trafficking, click-through destination validation in Google Campaign Manager 360, and SEO/SEM performance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.parent_brand_id IS 'Parent brand when this brand is a sub-brand or brand extension (e.g. Dove Men+Care under Dove). Null for top-level brands.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN client.brand.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.contract_deliverable IS 'Specific contractual deliverable committed under a SOW or agreement — such as a creative asset package, media plan, campaign report, or brand strategy deck. Captures deliverable name, description, due date, acceptance criteria, responsible team, delivery format, and current status (pending, in-progress, submitted, accepted, rejected). Bridges contract obligations to operational execution tracked in Workfront.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_id IS 'Unique identifier for the contractual deliverable. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client or advertiser for whom this deliverable is being produced.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract or Statement of Work (SOW) under which this deliverable is committed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.amendment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.amendment. Business justification: Contractual deliverables are frequently added, modified, or removed via amendments (scope changes). Adding amendment_id to contract_deliverable links each deliverable to the amendment that introduced';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Creative deliverables (ads, videos, copy) are produced for specific brands. Brand guidelines compliance, brand safety review, digital asset management, and brand portfolio reporting all require knowin';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the campaign or project to which this deliverable is associated, if applicable. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Deliverables consume resources from specific cost centers; finance tracks actual costs by deliverable for margin analysis and cost center performance reporting. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.dam_asset_id IS 'The identifier of the final deliverable asset stored in the Digital Asset Management (DAM) system. LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.creative.asset.asset_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.initiative_id IS 'Foreign key linking to project.initiative. Business justification: Contract deliverables are tracked in project management systems as initiatives/projects. Currently workfront_project_id is stored as an unlinked string. Normalizing to initiative_id FK enables joining LOGICAL REF -> work_mgmt_db.project.initiative.initiative_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Each contractual deliverable may be governed by a specific SLA defining its turnaround time, quality standard, revision cycle, or acceptance criteria. While contract_deliverable already has acceptance';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.sow_id IS 'Reference to the specific Statement of Work (SOW) that defines this deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.acceptance_criteria IS 'The specific criteria, standards, or requirements that must be met for the client to accept the deliverable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.acceptance_date IS 'The date on which the client formally accepted the deliverable as meeting contractual requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.actual_cost IS 'The actual total cost incurred to produce this deliverable, used for budget reconciliation and profitability analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.actual_hours IS 'The actual number of labor hours spent on completing this deliverable, tracked for billing and performance analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.billable_amount IS 'The amount that will be billed to the client for this deliverable, as specified in the contract or SOW.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.client_feedback IS 'Detailed feedback or comments provided by the client during the review process.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_description IS 'Detailed description of the deliverable scope, content, and specifications as outlined in the contract or SOW.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.contract_deliverable_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the deliverable (e.g., pending, in-progress, submitted, under review, accepted, rejected, on hold, cancelled). Code set: ref.contract_deliverable_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts associated with this deliverable (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.deliverable_code IS 'Unique business identifier or code for the deliverable, often used for tracking and billing purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.deliverable_name IS 'The business name or title of the deliverable as specified in the contract (e.g., ''Q1 Brand Strategy Deck'', ''Creative Asset Package - Summer Campaign'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.deliverable_type IS 'Classification of the deliverable by type (e.g., creative asset, media plan, campaign report, brand strategy deck, analytics dashboard). Code set: ref.deliverable_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.delivery_format IS 'The file format or medium in which the deliverable will be provided (e.g., PDF, PowerPoint, video file, HTML, ZIP archive). Code set: ref.delivery_format.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.delivery_method IS 'The method or channel through which the deliverable will be transmitted to the client (e.g., email, file share, DAM platform, physical delivery, client portal).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.due_date IS 'The contractually committed date by which the deliverable must be completed and submitted to the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.estimated_cost IS 'The estimated total cost to produce this deliverable, including labor, materials, and third-party expenses.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.estimated_hours IS 'The estimated number of labor hours required to complete this deliverable, used for resource planning and budgeting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.internal_notes IS 'Internal notes or comments from the production team regarding the deliverable, not shared with the client.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.is_milestone IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this deliverable represents a major milestone in the contract or project timeline.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.priority IS 'The business priority level assigned to this deliverable, used for resource allocation and scheduling decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.rejection_reason IS 'The reason provided by the client for rejecting the deliverable, if applicable, used to guide revisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.requires_client_approval IS 'Boolean flag indicating whether this deliverable requires formal client approval before being considered complete.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.responsible_team IS 'The internal team or department responsible for producing and delivering this deliverable (e.g., Creative, Media Planning, Analytics, Strategy).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.revision_number IS 'The current revision or version number of the deliverable, incremented with each resubmission or update.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.submission_date IS 'The actual date on which the deliverable was submitted to the client for review.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_deliverable.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.contract_insertion_order IS 'Formal IO (Insertion Order) record authorizing media spend with a specific publisher or vendor for a defined campaign flight. Captures IO number, media vendor reference, campaign reference, total authorized spend, flight start and end dates, placement specifications, rate type (CPM, CPC, CPA, flat fee), and IO status (draft, pending signature, executed, paused, cancelled). The authoritative transactional record linking media buying commitments to contractual obligations under a parent agreement. Supports media cost reconciliation and vendor payment authorization workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Unique identifier for the insertion order record. Primary key for the insertion order entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client advertiser on whose behalf this media spend is authorized.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: IOs in advertising are executed under a specific agency-client relationship governing commission rates, approval workflows, and billing. Agency-relationship-level IO spend reporting and commission rec';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Media insertion orders in advertising execute at brand level within advertisers. Tracking which brand each IO supports is essential for brand-level budget allocation, pacing reports, media mix analysi';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.campaign_id IS 'Reference to the parent campaign for which this insertion order authorizes media spend. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: An Insertion Order authorizes media spend at specific rates. While the IO captures execution-specific rate_amount and rate_type fields (which are kept as IO-specific overrides), linking to the governi';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: IOs authorize media spend against approved campaign budgets; budget management requires linking IO commitments to budgets for spend control and variance reporting. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.master_service_agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent master service agreement or contract under which this insertion order is executed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.media_insertion_order. Business justification: Contract IOs and media IOs represent the same business artifact from contract management vs. media execution perspectives. Linking enables reconciliation between contract commitments and media executi LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.media_insertion_order.media_insertion_order_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Insertion Orders are often executed under a specific Statement of Work that defines the scope and deliverables. N:1 relationship (many IOs can be under one SOW). No reverse FK exists. This links media';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.supplier_id IS 'Reference to the publisher or media vendor with whom this insertion order establishes a media buying commitment. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.agency_commission_rate IS 'The percentage commission rate earned by the agency on media spend under this insertion order, typically ranging from 0% to 20%.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.billing_contact_email IS 'Email address of the billing contact for invoice delivery and payment-related communications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.billing_contact_name IS 'Name of the primary billing contact responsible for invoice processing and payment authorization for this insertion order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.buying_method IS 'The method by which media inventory is purchased under this insertion order. RTB (Real-Time Bidding) indicates auction-based programmatic buying.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.cancellation_policy IS 'Terms and conditions governing cancellation or early termination of the insertion order, including notice periods and financial penalties.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.committed_clicks IS 'The total number of clicks committed or guaranteed under this insertion order for CPC-based campaigns. Null for non-click-based rate types.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.committed_conversions IS 'The total number of conversions or acquisitions committed under this insertion order for CPA-based campaigns. Null for non-conversion-based rate types.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.committed_impressions IS 'The total number of ad impressions committed or guaranteed by the media vendor under this insertion order. Null for non-guaranteed or performance-based deals.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this insertion order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.flight_end_date IS 'The date when the media campaign flight ends and ad serving authorization under this insertion order expires.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.flight_start_date IS 'The date when the media campaign flight begins and ad serving is authorized to commence under this insertion order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_approved_date IS 'The date when the insertion order was approved by the media vendor, authorizing campaign setup and trafficking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_name IS 'Human-readable descriptive name for the insertion order, typically including campaign reference and media vendor for easy identification.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_number IS 'The externally-known unique business identifier for this insertion order, used in communications with media vendors and internal tracking systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_signed_date IS 'The date when the insertion order was executed and signed by all required parties, establishing the binding commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the insertion order in the approval and execution workflow. Code set: ref.io_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_submitted_date IS 'The date when the insertion order was submitted to the media vendor for review and approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.io_type IS 'Classification of the insertion order based on the media buying model and inventory commitment type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.make_good_policy IS 'Terms governing make-good provisions when the media vendor fails to deliver committed impressions or performance metrics, including remediation options.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.media_channel IS 'The primary media channel or platform type for this insertion order. OOH (Out-of-Home), DOOH (Digital Out-of-Home), OTT (Over-the-Top), CTV (Connected TV). Code set: ref.media_channel.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.notes IS 'Free-form notes capturing additional terms, special instructions, or contextual information relevant to this insertion order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.payment_terms IS 'The agreed payment terms specifying when payment is due after invoice receipt (e.g., Net 30 means payment due within 30 days).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.placement_specifications IS 'Detailed specifications for ad placements including ad formats, sizes, positions, targeting criteria, and creative requirements as agreed with the media vendor.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.rate_amount IS 'The unit rate or price associated with the rate type (e.g., $5.00 CPM, $0.50 CPC). Precision supports fractional cent pricing common in programmatic media.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.rate_type IS 'The pricing model used for this insertion order. CPM (Cost Per Mille), CPC (Cost Per Click), CPA (Cost Per Acquisition), CPV (Cost Per View), CPCV (Cost Per Completed View), or other billing structure. Code set: ref.rate_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.third_party_ad_serving_fee IS 'Additional fee charged for third-party ad serving technology, tracking, and verification services associated with this insertion order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.total_authorized_spend IS 'The total budget amount authorized for media spend under this insertion order, representing the maximum financial commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.trafficking_contact_email IS 'Email address of the trafficking contact for campaign setup and creative asset coordination.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.trafficking_contact_name IS 'Name of the primary trafficking contact responsible for campaign setup, creative delivery, and ad serving coordination.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable. MVM column: created_by_user.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_insertion_order.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by_user.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.contract_rate_card IS 'Negotiated pricing schedule attached to a client agreement or vendor contract — defining unit rates for agency services (hourly FTE rates by role, production cost rates, media commission percentages) or vendor media inventory pricing (CPM floors, CPC rates, flat placement fees). Captures rate card version, effective date range, currency, rate type, and approval status. The SSOT for contractual pricing used in billing reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Unique identifier for the contract rate card. Primary key for this entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: Rate cards are channel-scoped (e.g., a digital rate card vs. broadcast rate card). Linking contract_rate_card to ad_channel enables channel-specific rate card lookup during media planning and buying. LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.ad_channel.ad_channel_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.advertiser_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.advertiser. Business justification: Rate cards in advertising are negotiated per advertiser. Direct advertiser-level rate card linkage enables advertiser pricing governance, rate card audits, and pricing reports without joining through';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Rate cards are negotiated as part of the agency-client relationship and govern fees across all work under that relationship. Linking rate card to agency_relationship enables relationship-level pricing';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract or agreement to which this rate card is attached. Links to the master contract entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: Brand-specific rate cards are common in advertising — different brands under the same advertiser may have distinct negotiated rates. Brand-level rate card management and pricing reports require this d';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Rate cards define billing rates that vary by cost center (creative vs. strategy teams have different overhead structures); finance uses this for margin calculation. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Contract rate cards represent pricing negotiated with a specific vendor. Linking contract_rate_card.supplier_id enables vendor rate management, rate compliance auditing, and spend analysis by vendor — LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.vendor_rate_card. Business justification: Negotiated contract rate cards are derived from vendor-published rate cards. This link enables rate negotiation tracking — comparing contracted rates against vendor''s published rates — a standard proc LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.vendor_rate_card.vendor_rate_card_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the person or role who approved this rate card for use. Supports approval audit trail.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.approved_date IS 'Date when this rate card was formally approved for use. Supports approval audit trail and compliance tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.audience_segment IS 'Target audience segment or demographic to which this rate applies, such as ''Adults 18-34'', ''High-Income Households'', ''B2B Decision Makers''. Supports audience-based pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.base_rate IS 'The standard or base rate amount for this rate card entry, before any adjustments, discounts, or surcharges. Precision supports fractional currency units and CPM calculations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.billing_frequency IS 'How often charges under this rate card are invoiced: weekly, biweekly, monthly, quarterly, milestone (upon reaching project milestones), on_completion (at project end), or custom (bespoke schedule). Code set: ref.billing_frequency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.contract_rate_card_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the rate card: draft (being prepared), pending_approval (submitted for review), approved (authorized but not yet effective), active (currently in force), suspended (temporarily inactive), expired (past effective period), superseded (replaced by newer version). Code set: ref.contract_rate_card_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all rates in this rate card (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Ensures consistent currency handling in multi-currency environments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.discount_percentage IS 'Negotiated discount percentage applied to the base rate, expressed as a percentage (e.g., 15.00 for 15% discount). Supports volume discounts or client-specific pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.effective_end_date IS 'Date when this rate card expires and is no longer applicable. Nullable for open-ended rate cards.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.effective_start_date IS 'Date when this rate card becomes effective and applicable for billing. Supports time-bound pricing agreements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.geography_scope IS 'Geographic scope or market to which this rate card applies, such as ''USA'', ''EMEA'', ''APAC'', ''New York DMA'', ''Global''. Supports geo-specific pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.is_default IS 'Flag indicating whether this is the default rate card for the associated contract or service line. True if default, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.is_negotiable IS 'Flag indicating whether rates in this card are open to negotiation or are fixed. True if negotiable, False if fixed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.markup_percentage IS 'Agency markup or commission percentage applied to vendor costs or media spend, expressed as a percentage (e.g., 20.00 for 20% markup).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.maximum_rate IS 'Ceiling rate or maximum charge applicable under this rate card. Used for rate caps or maximum allowable charges.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.minimum_rate IS 'Floor rate or minimum charge applicable under this rate card. Used for CPM floors, minimum hourly charges, or minimum project fees.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional notes, special terms, conditions, or clarifications related to this rate card. Supports business context and exception handling.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.payment_terms_days IS 'Number of days from invoice date within which payment is due under this rate card (e.g., 30 for Net 30, 60 for Net 60).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.pricing_model IS 'The pricing structure used in this rate card: hourly (time-based), daily, monthly, per_unit (per deliverable), CPM (Cost Per Mille), CPC (Cost Per Click), CPA (Cost Per Acquisition), flat_fee (fixed price), commission_percentage (percentage of media spend), tiered (volume-based pricing), or custom (bespoke arrangement). Code set: ref.pricing_model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.rate_card_name IS 'Descriptive name of the rate card for business reference, such as ''Q1 2024 Agency Services Rate Card'' or ''Premium Media Inventory Pricing''.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.rate_card_number IS 'Business identifier for the rate card, typically used in invoicing and billing reconciliation. Format: RC- followed by alphanumeric code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.rate_card_type IS 'Classification of the rate card by its purpose: agency_services (hourly FTE rates by role), media_inventory (CPM/CPC rates for ad placements), production (creative production cost rates), vendor_services (third-party vendor pricing), commission (media commission percentages), or hybrid (combination of multiple types).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.rate_category IS 'Business classification or grouping for the rates in this card, such as ''Senior Creative Staff'', ''Digital Media Placements'', ''Video Production Services'', or ''Programmatic Inventory''. Supports rate organization and reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.role_level IS 'For agency services rate cards, the seniority or role level to which this rate applies, such as ''Junior Designer'', ''Senior Account Director'', ''Executive Creative Director''. Supports role-based billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.service_line IS 'The agency service line or practice area covered by this rate card, such as ''Creative Services'', ''Media Planning'', ''Digital Strategy'', ''Production'', ''Analytics''. Supports service-based rate organization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.unit_of_measure IS 'The unit by which the rate is measured and billed: hour (hourly rate), day (daily rate), month (monthly retainer), impression (per 1000 impressions for CPM), click (per click for CPC), acquisition (per conversion for CPA), unit (per deliverable), project (per project), percentage (commission), or flat (one-time fee). Code set: ref.unit_of_measure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.version_number IS 'Version identifier for the rate card, supporting version control and change tracking. Format: v1.0, v2.1, etc.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.volume_tier IS 'Volume-based pricing tier identifier for tiered rate cards, such as ''Tier 1: 0-100K impressions'', ''Tier 2: 100K-500K impressions''. Supports tiered pricing models.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.contract_rate_card.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.rate_card_line IS 'Individual line-item entry within a rate card defining the unit price for a specific service, role, or media placement type. Captures line item code, service or role description, unit of measure (hour, impression, click, placement), unit rate, volume tier thresholds, discount percentage, and effective date range. Enables granular billing calculations and spend reconciliation against contracted rates.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.rate_card_line_id IS 'Primary key for rate_card_line';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.ad_channel_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_channel. Business justification: Rate card lines are structured by channel (digital, broadcast, OOH). Linking rate_card_line to ad_channel enables channel-specific rate enforcement during media buying and supports channel-level rate LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.ad_channel.ad_channel_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.ad_format_id IS 'Foreign key linking to media.ad_format. Business justification: Rate card lines are priced by ad format (e.g., :30 video spot vs. 300x250 display). Linking rate_card_line to ad_format enables format-specific rate validation during media buying and supports rate ca LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.media.ad_format.ad_format_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Reference to the parent rate card document that contains this line item. Links this line to the master rate card agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.approval_status IS 'Approval workflow status for this rate card line. Tracks whether pricing has been reviewed and authorized by appropriate stakeholders.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the person who approved this rate card line item. Supports audit trail and accountability for pricing decisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.approved_timestamp IS 'Date and time when this rate card line item was approved. Provides temporal audit trail for pricing authorization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.billing_frequency IS 'Cadence at which this line item is invoiced to the client. Aligns billing cycles with contract terms and cash flow management. Code set: ref.billing_frequency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.cost_center_code IS 'Internal cost center or department code for financial allocation and profit and loss (P&L) tracking. Links rate card revenue to organizational units.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the unit rate (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP). Enables multi-currency rate card management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.discount_percentage IS 'Percentage discount applied to the unit rate for this line item. Used for volume discounts, promotional pricing, or negotiated rate reductions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.effective_end_date IS 'Date when this rate card line item expires or is superseded. Null for open-ended rates. Enables rate change management and historical tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.effective_start_date IS 'Date when this rate card line item becomes active and applicable for billing. Supports rate versioning and temporal pricing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.gl_account_code IS 'General ledger account code for revenue recognition. Maps rate card line items to chart of accounts for financial reporting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.is_retainer_eligible IS 'Indicates whether this line item can be included in retainer-based billing arrangements. Supports hybrid fee structures combining retainer and project-based work.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.is_taxable IS 'Indicates whether this line item is subject to sales tax or value-added tax (VAT). Drives tax calculation in billing systems.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.line_item_code IS 'Business identifier code for this rate card line item. Used for billing system integration and invoice reconciliation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.line_sequence_number IS 'Sequential ordering of this line item within the parent rate card. Determines display order in proposals and invoices.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.line_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of this rate card line item. Controls whether the line is available for use in proposals and billing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.markup_percentage IS 'Agency markup or commission percentage applied on top of base cost for pass-through expenses or media buys. Common in media buying and vendor management.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.maximum_commitment_quantity IS 'Maximum volume or hours available for this line item under the contract terms. Null if no cap applies. Manages scope and resource allocation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.minimum_commitment_quantity IS 'Minimum volume or hours the client must purchase for this line item under the contract terms. Null if no minimum applies. Enforces contractual commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional context, special terms, or clarifications related to this rate card line item. Supports operational communication and edge case documentation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.overage_rate IS 'Rate charged for usage exceeding the maximum commitment quantity. Typically higher than the standard unit rate. Null if no overage pricing applies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.role_title IS 'Job title or role designation for labor-based rate card lines (e.g., Senior Art Director, Media Planner, Account Executive). Null for non-labor items.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.seniority_level IS 'Experience tier for labor-based rate card lines. Determines rate differential based on expertise and responsibility level.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.service_description IS 'Detailed description of the service, role, or media placement type covered by this line item. Provides clarity on scope and deliverables.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.service_type IS 'Category of service or deliverable covered by this rate card line. Classifies the type of work being priced.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.tax_category_code IS 'Tax classification code for this line item. Used by financial systems to apply correct tax rates and comply with jurisdictional tax rules.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.unit_of_measure IS 'The unit by which this service or media placement is quantified and billed (e.g., hourly rate, cost per thousand impressions, flat fee per placement). Code set: ref.unit_of_measure.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.unit_rate IS 'The base price charged per unit of measure. Core pricing element used for billing calculations and budget forecasting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.volume_tier_threshold_max IS 'Maximum quantity threshold for volume-based pricing tier. Null for open-ended top tier. Defines upper bound of pricing tier range.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.volume_tier_threshold_min IS 'Minimum quantity threshold for volume-based pricing tier. Null if no volume discounting applies. Used with volume_tier_threshold_max to define tier ranges.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.rate_card_line.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.agreement IS 'Master record for all commercial agreements between the agency and its clients or media vendors — including MSAs (Master Service Agreements), SOWs (Statements of Work), IOs (Insertion Orders), vendor media supply agreements, technology licenses, and production services contracts. Captures contract type (client or vendor), counterparty reference, status, effective and expiry dates, governing law, jurisdiction, auto-renewal flags, notice periods, total committed value, and the owning account team. Serves as the SSOT for all contractual relationships — both client-facing and supply-side — and is the anchor entity for the contract domain.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.agreement_id IS 'Unique identifier for the commercial agreement. Primary key for the agreement entity.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client advertiser party to this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: Master service agreements are budgeted and tracked against specific cost centers for P&L management, overhead allocation, and profitability analysis in agency operations. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.parent_agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent or master agreement if this is a child agreement (e.g., SOW under an MSA, Amendment to an IO). Nullable for top-level agreements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Master Service Agreements in advertising are negotiated with specific vendors/suppliers. Linking agreement.supplier_id enables vendor contract portfolio management, renewal tracking, and compliance re LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.agreement_number IS 'Externally-known business identifier for the agreement, used in client communications and invoicing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.agreement_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the agreement. Code set: ref.agreement_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.agreement_type IS 'Classification of the commercial agreement. MSA = Master Service Agreement, SOW = Statement of Work, IO = Insertion Order, RFP = Request for Proposal, RFI = Request for Information. Code set: ref.agreement_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.approval_date IS 'Date when internal approval was granted to execute this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the internal authority who approved this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.auto_renewal_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement automatically renews at expiry unless terminated.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.compliance_review_date IS 'Date of the most recent compliance or legal review of this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.confidentiality_clause_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement includes a confidentiality or non-disclosure provision.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.contract_owner IS 'Name or identifier of the individual responsible for ongoing management and compliance of this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.counterparty_type IS 'Indicates whether the agreement is with a client (revenue-generating), vendor (cost-generating), or strategic partner.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary values in this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.deliverables_summary IS 'High-level summary of key deliverables, milestones, or outputs expected under this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.dispute_resolution_method IS 'Agreed mechanism for resolving disputes arising from this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.document_storage_url IS 'URL or file path to the signed agreement document in the Digital Asset Management (DAM) or document management system.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.effective_date IS 'Date when the agreement becomes legally binding and enforceable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.exclusivity_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement grants exclusive rights to the agency or client within a defined scope or territory.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.expiry_date IS 'Date when the agreement terminates. Nullable for open-ended agreements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.governing_law IS 'Legal jurisdiction whose laws govern the interpretation and enforcement of this agreement (e.g., State of New York, England and Wales).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.indemnity_clause_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement includes an indemnity provision protecting one or both parties from third-party claims.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.liability_cap_amount IS 'Maximum liability amount either party can be held responsible for under this agreement. Nullable if no cap applies.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.next_review_date IS 'Scheduled date for the next periodic review or renewal discussion of this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.notes IS 'Free-text field for additional comments, special terms, or internal notes about this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.payment_terms_days IS 'Number of days from invoice date within which payment is due (e.g., Net 30, Net 60).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.performance_bonus_clause_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement includes performance-based bonus or incentive provisions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.pricing_model IS 'Commercial pricing structure for this agreement. CPM = Cost Per Mille, CPC = Cost Per Click, CPA = Cost Per Acquisition. Code set: ref.pricing_model.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.renewal_notice_period_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required to prevent auto-renewal or to initiate renewal negotiation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.scope_of_work_description IS 'Detailed description of the services, deliverables, and work products covered by this agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.signed_date IS 'Date when all parties executed the agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.sla_included_flag IS 'Indicates whether the agreement includes defined Service Level Agreements with performance targets and penalties.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.termination_date IS 'Actual date when the agreement was terminated, if applicable. Nullable for active agreements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.termination_notice_period_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required for either party to terminate the agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.termination_reason IS 'Explanation or business reason for early termination of the agreement, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.total_committed_value IS 'Total monetary value committed under this agreement over its full term. For client agreements, represents expected revenue; for vendor agreements, represents committed spend.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.agreement.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.amendment IS 'Formal change record modifying an existing agreement, SOW, or IO — capturing scope changes, budget adjustments, timeline extensions, or term revisions. Each amendment records the parent contract reference, amendment number, change type, original value, revised value, effective date, reason for change, and approval chain. Maintains a complete audit trail of all contractual modifications throughout the agreement lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.amendment_id IS 'Unique identifier for the contract amendment record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract, Statement of Work (SOW), Master Service Agreement (MSA), or Insertion Order (IO) being amended.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.campaign_id IS 'Foreign key linking to campaign.campaign. Business justification: Amendments to insertion orders or SOWs frequently adjust campaign budgets, timelines, or scope. Linking amendment→campaign enables budget reconciliation, change order tracking, and campaign financial LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.campaign.campaign.campaign_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Amendments can modify Insertion Orders (budget changes, flight date extensions, placement adjustments). N:1 relationship (many amendments can apply to one IO). No reverse FK exists. This allows tracki';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Amendments frequently modify pricing terms, which may involve updating or replacing a rate card. Adding contract_rate_card_id to amendment allows tracking which rate card was introduced or modified by';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Amendments can modify SLA terms — e.g., changing performance targets, penalty thresholds, or measurement methodologies. Adding sla_id to amendment allows tracking which SLA record was affected by the';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Amendments can modify SOWs (scope changes, deliverable adjustments) in addition to modifying master agreements. N:1 relationship (many amendments can apply to one SOW). No reverse FK exists. This allo';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.superseded_by_amendment_id IS 'Reference to a subsequent amendment that supersedes or replaces this amendment, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.agency_signatory_name IS 'Full name of the agency representative who signed the amendment on behalf of the agency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.agency_signatory_title IS 'Job title or role of the agency representative who signed the amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.amendment_number IS 'Sequential or hierarchical amendment identifier (e.g., A-001, Amendment 1, 2024-A-03) used for external reference and tracking.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.amendment_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the amendment in the approval and execution workflow.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.amendment_type IS 'Classification of the amendment based on the nature of the contractual change being made.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.approval_date IS 'Date on which the amendment received formal approval from the authorized approver.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the individual or authority who approved the amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.budget_delta_amount IS 'The net change in budget amount resulting from the amendment (revised minus original).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.change_description IS 'Detailed narrative describing the specific contractual changes, modifications, or adjustments being made through this amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.change_reason IS 'Business justification or rationale for the amendment, explaining why the contractual modification is necessary.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.client_signatory_name IS 'Full name of the client representative who signed the amendment on behalf of the client organization.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.client_signatory_title IS 'Job title or role of the client representative who signed the amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary amounts in this amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.document_url IS 'URL or file path to the signed amendment document stored in the Digital Asset Management (DAM) system or document repository.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.effective_date IS 'Date on which the amendment terms become binding and enforceable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.execution_date IS 'Date on which all required parties signed and executed the amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.expiration_date IS 'Date on which the amendment terms expire or are no longer applicable, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.legal_review_completed IS 'Indicates whether the required legal review has been completed for this amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.legal_review_date IS 'Date on which the legal review of the amendment was completed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.legal_review_required IS 'Indicates whether the amendment requires formal legal review before execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.notes IS 'Additional free-form notes, comments, or internal observations related to the amendment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.original_budget_amount IS 'The original contracted budget amount before the amendment, if the amendment involves budget changes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.original_end_date IS 'The original contract end date before the amendment, if the amendment involves timeline changes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.original_value IS 'The original contractual value, term, or specification before the amendment (stored as text to accommodate various data types).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.requested_by IS 'Name or identifier of the individual or party who initiated the amendment request.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.requested_date IS 'Date on which the amendment was formally requested by the client or agency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.revised_budget_amount IS 'The new contracted budget amount after the amendment is applied, if the amendment involves budget changes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.revised_end_date IS 'The new contract end date after the amendment is applied, if the amendment involves timeline changes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.revised_value IS 'The new contractual value, term, or specification after the amendment is applied (stored as text to accommodate various data types).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.version_number IS 'Version number of the amendment document, incremented with each revision during the draft and approval process.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.amendment.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.renewal IS 'Contract renewal event record tracking the lifecycle of agreement renewals — including auto-renewal triggers, manual renewal negotiations, pricing adjustments, and final outcome (renewed, renegotiated, lapsed, terminated). Captures renewal notice date, renewal effective date, prior term value, new term value, renewal type (auto, manual, renegotiation), responsible account manager, and client decision-maker. Supports proactive renewal pipeline management, revenue retention forecasting, and 90/60/30-day renewal alerting workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.renewal_id IS 'Unique identifier for the contract renewal event record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: Contract renewals in advertising are directly tied to agency-client relationship reviews. When an AOR relationship is up for renewal, the contract renewal process is triggered. Relationship-level rene';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract being renewed. Links this renewal event to the master agreement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.amendment_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.amendment. Business justification: In agency practice, a contract renewal is frequently formalized through an amendment to the existing agreement rather than a new standalone agreement. Adding amendment_id to renewal links the renewal';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: Contract renewals typically involve rate renegotiation, resulting in a new or revised rate card. Adding contract_rate_card_id to renewal links the renewal event to the rate card that will govern the r';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.finance_budget_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.finance_budget. Business justification: Contract renewals in advertising require a new or extended budget allocation. Linking renewal to finance_budget enables finance teams to confirm budget availability before renewal approval and support LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.finance_budget.finance_budget_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.sla_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sla. Business justification: Renewals often involve SLA renegotiation — performance targets may be raised, penalty structures revised, or new metrics introduced. Adding sla_id to renewal links the renewal event to the SLA record';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Renewals can be specific to SOWs (renewing a specific scope of work under a master agreement). N:1 relationship (many renewals can relate to one SOW). No reverse FK exists. This allows tracking SOW-le';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: Contract renewals are managed per vendor relationship. Linking renewal.supplier_id enables vendor renewal pipeline reporting, churn risk analysis by supplier, and preferred vendor tier decisions — a n LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.alert_sent_flag IS 'Indicates whether automated renewal alerts (90/60/30-day notifications) were successfully sent to the account team. True if alerts sent, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.approval_date IS 'Date when internal approval was granted for this renewal. Null if no approval was required.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.approval_required_flag IS 'Indicates whether this renewal required executive or legal approval due to value threshold, term length, or risk factors. True if approval required, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.auto_renewal_clause_flag IS 'Indicates whether the renewed contract includes an automatic renewal clause for the next term. True if auto-renewal is enabled, False if manual renewal required.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.churn_risk_flag IS 'Indicates whether this renewal was flagged as high churn risk based on client health indicators, payment issues, or competitive threats. True if at-risk, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.competitive_threat_flag IS 'Indicates whether the renewal process involved known competitive pressure or client evaluation of alternative agencies. True if competitive threat identified, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary values in this renewal record (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.decision_date IS 'Date when the client or vendor formally communicated their renewal decision (renew, renegotiate, or decline).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.effective_date IS 'Date when the renewed contract terms become binding and the new contract period begins. Typically aligns with the expiration date of the prior term.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.negotiation_end_date IS 'Date when renewal negotiations concluded, either with agreement or termination of discussions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.negotiation_start_date IS 'Date when formal renewal negotiations began with the client. Marks the transition from renewal notice to active discussion phase.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.new_term_end_date IS 'End date of the renewed contract term. Defines the duration of the new agreement period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.new_term_start_date IS 'Start date of the renewed contract term. Typically matches renewal_effective_date but may differ if there is a gap or overlap period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.new_term_value IS 'Total contract value of the renewed term, expressed in the contract currency. Captures pricing adjustments, scope changes, or inflationary increases.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.notes IS 'Free-text field for account team notes, client feedback, negotiation highlights, or special considerations related to this renewal event.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.notice_date IS 'Date when the renewal notice was sent to the client or vendor, triggering the renewal evaluation period. Critical for tracking compliance with contractual notice requirements (e.g., 90-day notice clauses).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.outcome IS 'Final result of the renewal process: renewed (client accepted renewal on existing or similar terms), renegotiated (client renewed with material changes), lapsed (client did not respond or declined passively), terminated (client actively ended relationship).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.pricing_model_change_flag IS 'Indicates whether the renewal involved a change to the pricing model (e.g., shift from CPM to CPA, or from fixed fee to performance-based). True if pricing model changed, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.prior_term_end_date IS 'End date of the contract term that is being renewed. Marks the expiration of the prior agreement and the trigger point for renewal evaluation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.prior_term_start_date IS 'Start date of the contract term that is being renewed. Used to calculate term length and renewal cycle metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.prior_term_value IS 'Total contract value of the term being renewed, expressed in the contract currency. Used to calculate renewal rate and revenue retention metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.probability_score IS 'Predictive score (0-100) representing the likelihood of successful renewal at the time of renewal notice. Derived from client health metrics, engagement scores, and historical renewal patterns.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.reason IS 'Free-text explanation of the drivers behind the renewal outcome. Captures client feedback, competitive factors, performance issues, or strategic rationale.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.renewal_number IS 'Business-facing identifier for this renewal event, typically formatted as contract number plus renewal sequence (e.g., MSA-2024-001-R2).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.renewal_status IS 'Current lifecycle state of the renewal event: pending (renewal window opened, no action yet), in_negotiation (active discussions), approved (client committed), renewed (executed and effective), lapsed (client did not renew), terminated (client ended relationship), cancelled (renewal process aborted). Code set: ref.renewal_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.renewal_type IS 'Classification of the renewal mechanism: auto (automatic renewal per contract terms), manual (proactive renewal negotiation), renegotiation (renewal with material term changes), amendment (renewal with scope or pricing adjustments).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.scope_change_flag IS 'Indicates whether the renewal involved a change to the scope of services or deliverables (e.g., added channels, reduced markets, new service lines). True if scope changed, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.sow_updated_flag IS 'Indicates whether the renewal required an updated Statement of Work (SOW) document due to scope, deliverable, or Service Level Agreement (SLA) changes. True if SOW updated, False otherwise.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.value_change_amount IS 'Net change in contract value from prior term to new term (new_term_value minus prior_term_value). Positive values indicate upsell, negative values indicate downsell or discount.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.value_change_percentage IS 'Percentage change in contract value from prior term to new term, calculated as (value_change_amount / prior_term_value) * 100. Key metric for renewal pricing analysis.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: updated_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.renewal.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.sla IS 'Service Level Agreement record defining measurable performance commitments within a client or vendor contract — including creative turnaround times, campaign go-live SLAs, reporting delivery deadlines, platform uptime guarantees, and media trafficking response times. Captures SLA type, metric name, target value, measurement unit, measurement frequency, breach threshold, penalty mechanism (credit, fee reduction, termination right), and remediation terms. Supports contract compliance monitoring, QBR scorecards, and automated breach alerting.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sla_id IS 'Unique identifier for the service level agreement record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract or statement of work (SOW) that contains this SLA commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: SLAs in advertising frequently govern specific media buys at the IO level — e.g., impression delivery guarantees, viewability thresholds, brand safety commitments tied to a specific publisher IO. Whil';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: SLA performance is tracked by the cost center responsible for delivery; finance monitors SLA compliance costs and penalty exposure. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Service Level Agreements can be defined at SOW level with specific performance commitments for that scope of work. N:1 relationship (many SLAs can belong to one SOW). No reverse FK exists. This allows';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.supplier_id IS 'Foreign key linking to vendor.supplier. Business justification: SLAs in advertising are negotiated with specific vendors (ad servers, publishers, DSPs). Linking sla.supplier_id enables vendor SLA breach tracking, penalty enforcement, and supplier performance repor LOGICAL REF -> media_ops_db.vendor.supplier.supplier_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.approval_authority IS 'Role or individual who has authority to approve SLA modifications, waivers, or breach remediation plans.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.auto_renewal_flag IS 'Indicates whether this SLA automatically renews at the end of its term (true) or requires explicit renegotiation (false).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.baseline_measurement_period IS 'The time period over which the baseline performance was measured (e.g., ''Q4 2023'', ''Last 6 months'', ''Prior contract term'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.baseline_performance IS 'Historical or benchmark performance level used as a reference point for setting the SLA target, captured at contract negotiation.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.breach_threshold IS 'The performance level at which an SLA breach is triggered, may differ from target to allow tolerance (e.g., target 24 hours, breach at 30 hours).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.breach_threshold_unit IS 'Unit of measure for the breach threshold value.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.client_acceptance_date IS 'The date when the client formally accepted and signed off on this SLA commitment.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.compliance_tracking_enabled IS 'Indicates whether automated compliance monitoring and breach alerting is enabled for this SLA (true) or manual tracking only (false).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.effective_end_date IS 'The date when this SLA commitment expires or is superseded, nullable for open-ended commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.effective_start_date IS 'The date when this SLA commitment becomes active and enforceable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.escalation_contact IS 'Name or role of the individual or team to be notified when an SLA breach occurs or is imminent.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.exclusions IS 'Circumstances or conditions explicitly excluded from SLA measurement (e.g., force majeure, client-caused delays, third-party platform outages, holiday periods).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.last_review_date IS 'The most recent date when this SLA was reviewed during a quarterly business review (QBR) or contract review cycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.measurement_frequency IS 'How often the SLA performance is measured and reported (per transaction, daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, annual).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.measurement_methodology IS 'Detailed description of how the SLA metric is calculated, what data sources are used, and any rounding or aggregation rules applied.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.measurement_unit IS 'Unit of measure for the target value (hours, business days, calendar days, percentage, minutes, count).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.metric_name IS 'The specific measurable performance indicator being tracked (e.g., ''Response Time'', ''Delivery Time'', ''Uptime Percentage'', ''Approval Cycle Duration'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.next_review_date IS 'The scheduled date for the next formal review of this SLA commitment, typically aligned with QBR cycles.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.notes IS 'Additional context, clarifications, or special conditions related to this SLA that do not fit in structured fields.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.penalty_amount IS 'The monetary value or percentage of the penalty applied per breach occurrence, if applicable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.penalty_currency_code IS 'ISO 4217 three-letter currency code for the penalty amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.penalty_mechanism IS 'The contractual remedy applied when an SLA is breached (service credit, fee reduction, termination right, penalty payment, none).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.remediation_terms IS 'Detailed description of the corrective actions, escalation procedures, and resolution commitments when an SLA breach occurs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.reporting_schedule IS 'Frequency at which SLA performance reports are delivered to the client or stakeholders (real-time, daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, on-demand).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sla_code IS 'Business identifier or code for the SLA, often referenced in contract documents and quarterly business reviews (QBRs).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sla_name IS 'Human-readable name of the SLA commitment (e.g., ''Creative Turnaround Time'', ''Campaign Go-Live SLA'', ''Reporting Delivery Deadline'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sla_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the SLA (active, suspended, expired, terminated, draft, under review).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.sla_type IS 'Category of SLA defining the nature of the performance commitment (creative turnaround, campaign go-live, reporting delivery, platform uptime, trafficking response, client approval).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.target_value IS 'The committed performance target value that must be met or exceeded (e.g., 24 hours, 99.9 percent, 2 business days).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sla.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_by.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.sow IS 'Statement of Work entity capturing the detailed scope, deliverables, milestones, timelines, and pricing for a specific client engagement under a parent MSA or standalone agreement. Tracks SOW number, version, approval status, total value, start and end dates, billing model (fixed-fee, T&M, retainer), and the responsible account manager. Supports Proposal Development and Pitching and Budget Management processes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_id IS 'Unique identifier for the Statement of Work record. Primary key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.agency_relationship_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.agency_relationship. Business justification: SOWs are executed under a specific agency-client AOR relationship governing commission rates, scope, and approval workflows. Linking SOW to agency_relationship enables relationship-level SOW tracking';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent Master Service Agreement under which this SOW is executed. Null if this is a standalone SOW without a parent MSA.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.brand_id IS 'Foreign key linking to client.brand. Business justification: SOWs in advertising are scoped to a specific brand — media budgets, deliverables, and fee structures are brand-specific. Brand-level SOW reporting and budget reconciliation require this link. A domain';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.contract_rate_card_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_rate_card. Business justification: A Statement of Work may reference a specific rate card that governs the pricing for its deliverables and services. While the rate card is linked to the parent agreement, different SOWs under the same';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.cost_center_id IS 'Foreign key linking to finance.cost_center. Business justification: SOWs are executed within cost center budgets; finance tracks SOW spend by cost center for profitability analysis and resource allocation decisions. LOGICAL REF -> erp_db.finance.cost_center.cost_center_id (not enforced: cross-system).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the specific advertiser entity under the client organization. May differ from client_id in holding company structures.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_client_advertiser_id IS 'Reference to the client or advertiser for whom this SOW is executed. Links to the client master record.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.agency_fee_amount IS 'Total agency service fees for the SOW, excluding media costs and third-party pass-throughs. Represents the agency''s revenue from this engagement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.approval_date IS 'Date when the SOW was formally approved by the client and agency, making it legally binding.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.auto_renewal_flag IS 'Indicates whether the SOW automatically renews unless either party provides notice of termination. True if auto-renewal clause exists.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.billing_model IS 'Pricing structure for the SOW. Determines how the client is invoiced (fixed price, hourly rates, monthly retainer, media commission, performance incentives, or combination).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.confidentiality_clause IS 'Text of the confidentiality and non-disclosure provisions governing how both parties handle sensitive information shared during the engagement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.currency_code IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for all monetary values in this SOW (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.deliverables_summary IS 'High-level summary of key deliverables expected under this SOW (e.g., ''3 TV spots, 10 digital banners, monthly performance reports'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.effective_end_date IS 'Date when the SOW expires or the engagement concludes. Null for open-ended retainer agreements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.effective_start_date IS 'Date when the SOW becomes effective and work may commence. Marks the beginning of the engagement period.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.intellectual_property_ownership IS 'Specifies who owns the intellectual property rights to work created under this SOW (client owns all, agency retains rights, shared ownership, or work-for-hire arrangement).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.invoicing_frequency IS 'Cadence at which the client will be invoiced under this SOW. Aligns with billing model and cash flow requirements.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.media_budget_amount IS 'Total media spend budget allocated under this SOW for media buying and placement. Excludes agency fees and production costs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.payment_terms IS 'Contractual payment terms specifying when and how invoices are to be paid (e.g., ''Net 30'', ''Net 60'', ''50% upfront, 50% on completion'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.performance_bonus_amount IS 'Maximum potential performance bonus amount payable to the agency if all performance criteria are met. Null if no performance incentives exist.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.performance_bonus_criteria IS 'Description of performance metrics and thresholds that trigger bonus payments to the agency (e.g., ''ROAS exceeds 5:1'', ''Campaign CTR above 2%'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.production_budget_amount IS 'Total budget allocated for creative production, including video, photography, design, and other content creation costs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.renewal_notice_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required to terminate or opt out of renewal. Null if no renewal option exists.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.renewal_option_flag IS 'Indicates whether the SOW includes an option for renewal or extension beyond the initial term. True if renewal clause exists.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.scope_of_work IS 'Comprehensive description of all services, deliverables, and activities included in the SOW. Defines what is in-scope and out-of-scope.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sla_deliverable_turnaround_days IS 'Standard number of business days committed for deliverable turnaround under normal circumstances. Part of service level commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sla_response_time_hours IS 'Maximum number of hours the agency commits to respond to client requests or issues under this SOW. Part of service level commitments.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_description IS 'Detailed narrative description of the SOW scope, objectives, and high-level deliverables. Provides context for the engagement.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_number IS 'Business-facing unique identifier for the SOW, typically formatted as SOW-XXXXXX. Used in client communications, invoicing, and contract references.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_status IS 'Current lifecycle status of the SOW. Tracks progression from draft through approval, execution, and closure. Code set: ref.sow_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.sow_type IS 'Classification of the SOW by engagement type. Determines billing model, resource allocation, and deliverable expectations. Code set: ref.sow_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.termination_clause IS 'Text of the termination provisions, specifying conditions under which either party may terminate the SOW and associated notice periods or penalties.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.title IS 'Descriptive title of the SOW, summarizing the engagement or campaign scope (e.g., ''Q1 2024 Brand Awareness Campaign'', ''Digital Media Planning Services'').';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.total_contract_value IS 'Total monetary value of the SOW across its entire duration, including all fees, media spend, and pass-through costs. Expressed in the contract currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.version_number IS 'Version identifier for the SOW document, typically in major.minor format (e.g., 1.0, 2.1). Incremented with each amendment or revision.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: last_modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.sow.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';

COMMENT ON TABLE contract.term IS 'Granular terms and conditions clauses attached to an agreement or SOW — including payment terms (net-30, net-60), IP ownership clauses, confidentiality obligations, indemnification provisions, termination-for-convenience rights, and audit rights. Each term record captures clause type, clause text, effective date, negotiated flag, and approval status. Enables clause-level compliance tracking and legal review workflows.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.term_id IS 'Primary key for term';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.agreement_id IS 'Reference to the parent contract or agreement to which this term belongs.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.contract_insertion_order_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.contract_insertion_order. Business justification: Terms and conditions clauses can be attached to specific Insertion Orders (e.g., IO-specific cancellation terms, make-good provisions, trafficking requirements). While term already links to agreement';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.sow_id IS 'Foreign key linking to contract.sow. Business justification: Terms and conditions can be specific to a SOW (not just agreement-level). N:1 relationship (many terms can belong to one SOW). No reverse FK exists. This allows SOW-specific terms to be tracked separa';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.amendment_count IS 'Number of times this term clause has been amended or modified since the original contract execution.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.approval_status IS 'Current approval state of the term clause within the contract review and approval workflow (e.g., draft, pending legal review, pending finance review, pending executive approval, approved, rejected, superseded). Code set: ref.approval_status.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.approved_by IS 'Name or identifier of the individual or role who provided final approval for this term clause.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.approved_date IS 'Date when the term clause received final approval and was authorized for inclusion in the executed contract.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.audit_frequency IS 'Specified frequency or trigger for audit rights when audit_rights_flag is True (e.g., annual, semi-annual, quarterly, upon request).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.audit_rights_flag IS 'Indicates whether this term grants audit rights to either party (True) or does not include audit provisions (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.auto_renewal_flag IS 'Indicates whether this term includes automatic renewal provisions (True) or requires explicit renewal action (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.clause_category IS 'High-level categorization of the clause into legal, commercial, operational, compliance, financial, or technical domains for organizational and reporting purposes.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.clause_summary IS 'Plain-language summary of the clause for business users, highlighting key obligations, rights, and implications.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.clause_text IS 'Full legal text of the term clause as negotiated and executed. Contains the complete wording of the contractual provision.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.clause_title IS 'Short descriptive title or heading of the term clause as it appears in the contract document.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.clause_type IS 'Classification of the term clause by its legal or commercial function (e.g., payment terms, IP ownership, confidentiality, indemnification, termination rights, audit rights, liability limitation, warranty, SLA, scope, deliverable, pricing, renewal). Code set: ref.clause_type.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.compliance_framework IS 'Name of the regulatory or compliance framework that governs this term (e.g., GDPR, CCPA, IAB Standards, MRC Guidelines, TAG Certification) when compliance_requirement_flag is True.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.compliance_requirement_flag IS 'Indicates whether this term clause is subject to regulatory compliance monitoring and reporting requirements (True) or is a standard commercial term (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.confidentiality_duration_years IS 'Number of years that confidentiality obligations remain in effect after contract termination when the clause type is confidentiality-related.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.effective_date IS 'Date when this specific term clause becomes binding and enforceable within the contract lifecycle.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.expiration_date IS 'Date when this term clause ceases to be in effect, if applicable. Null for terms that remain in force for the duration of the contract.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.indemnification_scope IS 'Description of the scope and limitations of indemnification obligations when the clause type is indemnification-related.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.intellectual_property_ownership IS 'Specifies the ownership model for intellectual property created under the contract when the clause type is IP-related (e.g., client owns, agency owns, joint ownership, work-for-hire, licensed).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.last_amended_date IS 'Date of the most recent amendment to this term clause.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.liability_cap_amount IS 'Maximum liability amount specified in the term clause when the clause type is liability limitation, expressed in the contract currency.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.liability_cap_currency IS 'Three-letter ISO 4217 currency code for the liability cap amount (e.g., USD, EUR, GBP).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.negotiated_flag IS 'Indicates whether this term was negotiated and modified from the standard template (True) or accepted as-is from the standard contract language (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.notes IS 'Additional notes, comments, or context regarding the term clause, including negotiation history, special considerations, or implementation guidance.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.payment_method IS 'Specified payment instrument or mechanism for financial settlement (e.g., wire transfer, ACH, check, credit card, EFT) when applicable to the term.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.payment_term_days IS 'Number of days for payment terms (e.g., net-30, net-60, net-90) when the clause type is payment-related.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.penalty_provision IS 'Description of financial or contractual penalties for non-compliance with the term, including service level breaches, late payments, or other violations.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.renewal_notice_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required to opt out of automatic renewal or to initiate renewal discussions.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.risk_level IS 'Assessment of the legal or financial risk associated with this term clause, used for prioritization of legal review and compliance monitoring.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.sequence IS 'Ordering or numbering of the term within the parent contract or Statement of Work (SOW), used to maintain clause hierarchy and presentation order.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.service_level_metric IS 'Name of the performance metric or Key Performance Indicator (KPI) specified in the service level term (e.g., response time, uptime percentage, delivery timeframe).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.service_level_target IS 'Target value or threshold for the service level metric (e.g., 99.9% uptime, 24-hour response time, 5-day delivery).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.standard_clause_flag IS 'Indicates whether this term is part of the organization''s standard contract template (True) or is a custom clause specific to this agreement (False).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.term_number IS 'Business identifier for the term clause, often used for legal reference and cross-referencing within contract documents.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.termination_notice_days IS 'Number of days advance notice required for contract termination when the clause type is termination-related (e.g., 30-day notice, 60-day notice).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.created_at IS 'Timestamp when the row was inserted. Set by default, immutable (enforced by audit trigger). MVM column: created_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.created_by IS 'Application user (session setting app.actor) or database role that inserted the row. Immutable.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.updated_at IS 'Timestamp of the last update. Maintained by the audit trigger. MVM column: modified_timestamp.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN contract.term.updated_by IS 'Application user or database role that last updated the row. Maintained by the audit trigger.';
